{"id":"000VNN","title":"Light Towers","author":"tigran","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-22T13:52:09+00:00","posted":"Heute, 11:44 Uhr","rules":"Hey everyone! Here is another puzzle with the dynamic distance rule. I do not know how to rate this puzzle (and the last one), because this rule may be foreign for some, but once understood the puzzle unravels pretty easily.\n\nRules\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply.\n\nArrows: Digits along an arrow sum up to the total in the circled cell.\n\nDynamic Distance: Two identical digits N may not be closer than √N to each other (distance < √N). Distance is measured between cell centers, with every cell being 1x1. (See the list at the end for the implications for each digit.)\n\nDynamic Fog: The puzzle is covered in Fog. Entering a correct digit will lift the fog in the cells that it \"sees\" (as described in the dynamic distance rule). No guessing is required.\n\nSolve in SudokuPad\n\nDistance rule implications:\n\n1 – none\n\n2 – orthogonally adjacent\n\n3, 4, 5 – additionally diagonally adjacent (chess king's move)\n\n6, 7, 8 – additionally chess knight's move\n\n9 – additionally 2 cells diagonally\n\n5 does not see a knight's move away because the distance is exactly √5, not less than.\n\n8 does not see 2 cells diagonally away because the distance is exactly √8, not less than.\n\nHint (highlight the box below to see):\n\nTry placing 9 in the center box. It is very restricted due to the dynamic distance rule.","solutionCode":"Row 1 from left to right","tags":["Sudoku","Arrows (Variante)","Distance (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/x25v3x8qnd","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/x25v3x8qnd","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["arrows","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-22T13:52:09+00:00"}